{color.GG}Fchmod {color.N}is a recursive permission management tool that applies chmod-style changes to selected files, directories, or symlinks.

Usage: {color.GG}fchmod {color.CC}<file|dir> --mode dxxxx:fxxxx:sxxxx [--only <file|dir|symlink>] [--ext <.ext>] [--norecursive]{color.N}

Example:
    {color.R}- {color.GG}fchmod {color.CC}mydir/ --mode d0644:f0755{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}fchmod {color.CC}mydir/ --mode f0755 --only file --ext .sh{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}fchmod {color.CC}myfile.py --mode 0755{color.N}